infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title RabbitMQ vs Kafka: two ends of one spectrum
  desc Smart-broker push with ack-and-delete vs dumb-broker pull over a replayable log
  compares
    - label RabbitMQ
      children
        - label Smart broker, dumb consumer
          desc Broker routes, pushes, tracks per-message acks
        - label Tens of thousands msg/sec
          desc Per queue; drops to low thousands when durable
        - label Sub-millisecond p50 latency
          desc Pushes each message as it arrives
        - label Deleted on ack
          desc No log to rewind — a consumed message is gone
        - label Rich content routing
          desc direct / fanout / topic / headers bindings
    - label Kafka
      children
        - label Dumb broker, smart consumer
          desc Broker stores ordered records, consumer pulls at its offset
        - label About 1 million msg/sec
          desc Per partition; batched sequential log writes
        - label 5 to 15 ms p50 latency
          desc Structural floor from batching
        - label Retained for replay
          desc New consumer group can read from offset zero
        - label No built-in routing
          desc Throughput and replay, not per-message control
theme
  palette #f59e0b #6366f1
